WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
A fed cell builds palmitate two carbons at a time.

2
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:07.760
Each turn costs one ATP and two NADPH.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.560
But the same cell also holds mitochondria that burn fat.

4
00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:17.000
So what stops new fat from being burned as fast as it is made?

5
00:00:20.483 --> 00:00:25.303
If both ran at once, the cell would build a chain, then tear it down, paying for

6
00:00:25.303 --> 00:00:31.823
both. Its separate places, carriers and electron pools make it possible to control

7
00:00:31.823 --> 00:00:33.343
each direction on its own.

8
00:00:34.723 --> 00:00:36.483
Building has one main control point.

9
00:00:37.517 --> 00:00:41.977
That point is ACC, the enzyme that makes malonyl CoA.

10
00:00:43.257 --> 00:00:46.537
Citrate, which piles up when fuel is plentiful, switches it on.

11
00:00:47.837 --> 00:00:53.857
So does insulin. Palmitoyl CoA, the finished product, switches it off, a clean

12
00:00:53.857 --> 00:00:54.857
feedback brake.

13
00:00:55.750 --> 00:01:02.010
AMPK, the cell's low-fuel sensor, also switches ACC off, by attaching a phosphate.

14
00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:07.990
Another enzyme, PP2A, removes the phosphate and turns it back on.

15
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.500
Now the elegant part.

16
00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.000
Malonyl CoA has a second job.

17
00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:20.600
It blocks CPT-I, the gate fat must pass to enter the mitochondrion and be burned.

18
00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.260
So the molecule that commits a cell to building also shuts the door on burning.

19
00:01:27.383 --> 00:01:29.363
ACC comes in two forms.

20
00:01:30.603 --> 00:01:34.343
ACC1 works in the cytoplasm and feeds the synthase.

21
00:01:35.463 --> 00:01:38.403
ACC2 sits on the mitochondrion itself.

22
00:01:39.763 --> 00:01:42.983
Why put a fat-building enzyme on the organelle that burns fat?

23
00:01:48.967 --> 00:01:51.387
Because that is where the blocker is made.

24
00:01:52.647 --> 00:01:58.177
Much of the malonyl CoA that blocks CPT-I comes from ACC2.

25
00:01:58.177 --> 00:02:02.587
ACC1's malonyl CoA is mainly a building block.

26
00:02:03.847 --> 00:02:05.727
ACC2's is mainly a signal.

27
00:02:06.817 --> 00:02:08.357
Follow a well-fed cell.

28
00:02:09.757 --> 00:02:14.517
Insulin and plentiful citrate push ACC on, and malonyl CoA rises.

29
00:02:15.897 --> 00:02:19.777
The synthase gets its extenders, and the CPT-I gate closes.

30
00:02:21.157 --> 00:02:23.757
A cell that is building fat tends not to burn it.

31
00:02:24.717 --> 00:02:28.777
So the answer to our question is one small molecule with two jobs.

32
00:02:29.957 --> 00:02:32.537
In the cytoplasm it is a brick for the chain.

33
00:02:33.857 --> 00:02:36.277
At the mitochondrion it is a lock on the door.

34
00:02:37.477 --> 00:02:39.877
So a cell tends not to build and burn at once.
